incident-bot: INCIDENT P2 — elevated 429 and latency spikes observed in hosted inference (us-east-1) starting ~1867501200. Affected: ~12 customers, bursty traffic patterns on streaming/generation routes, error surge to 8% 429s. Paging oncall-runtime and SRE.
oncall-runtime: Got it. I'm looking at autoscaler + quota checks. Initial quick check: node pool CPU fine, GPU utilization ~70%, but we're seeing new request rejection due to a per-customer burst limiter in the routing layer. Investigating whether fallback routing kicked in. Marking impact window and starting live mitigation discussion. @sre_anna can you triage policy side?
sre_anna: On it. I'm seeing a surge of small concurrent requests from a subset of API keys — traffic shaping thresholds (burst=100/sec) exceeded -> token-based throttles returning 429. Autoscaler didn't trigger because concurrent active connections were under threshold; this is a routing-level soft-throttle. Root cause likely a sudden customer-side fanout (clients opening multiple concurrent streams).
eng_client: Noted. We should coordinate a client-side mitigation message for SDKs ASAP. Recommend these immediate mitigations: reduce per-client concurrency, enforce idempotency keys, and apply exponential backoff with jitter on 429/5xx. Also advise honoring `Retry-After` when present. I'll draft guidance below.
paul_ops: For infra mitigation, propose temporary live changes: 1) Add a short-term server-side shaping: reduce per-key burst to 50% of normal for 30m, 2) enable a global soft-queue for streaming requests to smooth spikes, 3) disable a non-critical experimental feature (token-prefetch) to free routing capacity. Can we implement in next 3–5 minutes? @deploy-bot if config change ok
deploy-bot: Rolling config change: applying routing.burst_limit_pct=50 for tenant bucketers in us-east-1. Change queued and will deploy in 2 mins. (CI: OK) Reaction: :gear: 
sre_anna: Confirmed, applying temporary shaping. Also creating an alert rule suppress window for noisy keys to avoid paging storm for the same symptom.
support_jane: I'll prepare a short status note for affected customers: "Experiencing elevated error rates; working on throttling adjustments; recommended SDK mitigations included." Want to include exact client guidance — @eng_client can you paste the snippet?
eng_client: Paste incoming. Keep it short for SDK teams — copy/paste friendly.
eng_client: JS example (vanilla fetch) — exponential backoff + idempotency header:
```
async function callWithBackoff(url, body, maxAttempts = 6) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt < maxAttempts) {
    const idempotency = body.idempotencyKey || generateId();
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
          'Idempotency-Key': idempotency,
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
      });

      if (res.status === 429) {
        const ra = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
        const wait = ra ? parseInt(ra) * 1000 : Math.min(6000, 200 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
        // full jitter
        await sleep(Math.random() * wait);
        attempt++;
        continue;
      }

      if (res.ok) return await res.json();
      // for 5xx, apply same backoff
      if (res.status >= 500) {
        const wait = Math.min(6000, 200 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
        await sleep(Math.random() * wait);
        attempt++;
        continue;
      }

      // other 4xx -> surface to caller
      throw new Error(`Request failed: ${res.status}`);
    } catch (e) {
      attempt++;
      const wait = Math.min(6000, 200 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
      await sleep(Math.random() * wait);
    }
  }
  throw new Error('Max retry attempts reached');
}
```
eng_client: Key guidance summary (for SDK docs / quick notices):
- Honor `Retry-After` header when present.
- Exponential backoff with full jitter, base ~200ms, cap ~6s.
- Use stable Idempotency-Key per logical request to allow safe retries.
- Limit client-side concurrent streams per API key (recommend default 3 concurrent streaming generations).
- If using batch/queueing, prefer client-side paced batching instead of large fanout.
paul_ops: Ops note: We'll also push a temporary per-tenant quota reduction (burst windows) to reduce global tail. This should lower 429 rate quickly. If we see error drop <5% in 10m, we keep for 30m then roll to normal gradually.
oncall-runtime: Deployed routing change; initial metrics show 429s dropping from 8% -> 3.2% in first 90s. Streaming latency percentile also improving. Good signal. Keep watch for any customer-reported functional regressions due to disabled feature.
sre_anna: Adding a short checklist for on-call handoff: 1) Confirm 429s < 4% for 15m; 2) Confirm disabled feature didn't break essential flows; 3) Document mitigation ops run (change id, rollout id) in incident log; 4) If relapse, escalate to eng-runtime for capacity burst increases.
support_jane: Status update sent to affected customers: "We've applied temporary throttling adjustments and recommend SDK retry/backoff. We're monitoring closely and will update in 30 minutes." (link to status page: https://status.redwood.example/incidents/186750)
paul_ops: @paul_ops taking patch ownership for next shift. Handoff to @paul_ops at 06:00 UTC. Notes included in incident timeline.
oncall-runtime: For handoff — leaving runbook snippet: If 429s rise again, revert disabled feature off (re-enable token-prefetch) only after confirming capacity. Otherwise, extend shaping for another 30m and coordinate with customer success for high-value tenants.
eng_client: We'll also publish a short changelog entry in SDK repos with the guidance above and a `breaking` note that default concurrency recommendations are lowered temporarily. Add example patch for Python and JS soon.
deploy-bot: Routing config successful. Rollout id: r-2026-11-25-01. Reaction: :white_check_mark: 
support_jane: Affected customers acknowledged the status note, few asked for ETA — replied with "monitoring, next update in 30 min". No escalations yet.
oncall-runtime: Last check @1867501480: 429s steady ~2.9%, latency P95 improving. I'll leave the thread and hand off to @paul_ops. Everyone please react with :thumbsup: when you've read this handoff.
paul_ops: Acknowledged. Taking over monitoring and customer escalations. Thanks team. :thumbsup:
